<title>NETHERLANDS: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stocks rise.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stocks rise.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			30/1/97		  23/1/97		2/2/96</p>
<p>    Gasoline	550-575			525		   525</p>
<p>    Naphtha	     100		   75-100		    50</p>
<p>    Gas oil	   1,800		    1,900		 1,700</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	    400		  300-325	     375-400</p>
<p>    Jet kero	     20			 20		    15</p>
<p>Gasoline stocks rose with lots of incoming components readying to be built into cargoes for transatlantic shipment and with the contango offering an incentive to store.</p>
<p>Naphtha stocks were also slightly up as coasters arrived.</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks fell as IPE delivered material left for Belgium and down the Rhine.</p>
<p>Fuel oil stocks rose although some storage enquiries disappeared as a falling market gave few incentives to store and some were interested in keeping the market short to hike prices.</p>
<p>Jet fuel stocks changed little with some material heading to the gas oil pool.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5004</p>
</text>
